 ## Charges
 
-| Method | Path           | Success      |
-| ------ | -------------- | ------------ |
-| GET    | `/charges/:id` | `200` charge |
+| Method | Path                                               | Success                  |
+| ------ | -------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------ |
+| GET    | `/charges/:id`                                     | `200` charge             |
+| POST   | `/charges/:id/refunds` `{ amount_cents, reason? }` | `201` refund             |
+| GET    | `/charges/:id/refunds`                             | `200 { data: Refund[] }` |
 
 A charge has `amount_cents`, `status` (`succeeded` or `failed`), `failure_reason` and `gateway_reference` (both `null` when not applicable).
 
+### Refunds
+
+`createRefund` (`src/billing/refunds.ts`) records a partial or full refund of a charge. The money is returned by finance in the processor dashboard; the API keeps the record and writes a `charge.refunded` event.
+
+- `amount_cents` must be a positive integer (`400` otherwise).
+- Only `succeeded` charges can be refunded (`409 charge_not_refundable`).
+- The sum of all refunds of a charge never exceeds its `amount_cents`: a refund above the remaining amount is rejected with `422 refund_exceeds_charge` (`details.remaining_cents`).
+- Like every write, it requires `Idempotency-Key`; a replay returns the original refund and does not refund again.
+- `reason` is optional and stays `null` when not given.
+
